{"kind":"Article","sha256":"2d83a39c63373a82e7ca7394ff01361693515c62e1aaaa8a9845f63538e99146","slug":"arcane-toxicity","location":"/magic/arcane-toxicity.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Arcane Toxicity","github":"https://github.com/SkillWeaverNexus/skillweavernexus.github.io","keywords":[],"exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"arcane-toxicity.md","url":"/build/arcane-toxicity-67171ab92c2104f1f763de33910b4709.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"All magic comes with a cost. Channeling great forces through oneself slowly builds up a toxicity that if unchecked, can hurt or even kill you. SWM tracks this toxicity via Arcane Toxicity, or TOX for short.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"WZ02PvqPHK"}],"key":"q7O1jYIxYs"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every use of magic in the system (namely, spells, but also magical effects in general) will list an associated TOX score. This number describes both the amount of toxicity it imparts on the caster, but also serves as the spell’s `level’, capturing something about the intensity or scope of the effect.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"ZcmpJx6hBO"}],"key":"K7egSzhsKo"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ability to cast magic is open to any character in SWM, via the special “Arcane Initiate” feat in the Reasoning tree. We will colloquially refer to magic casters as ``mages’’ in this document, but any setting specific names or delinations could be further applied.","position":{"start":{"line":7,"column":1},"end":{"line":7,"column":1}},"key":"AdyKFMeAMr"}],"key":"uo6UliHGuH"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Threshold Values","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"Eqy2ChDNlo"}],"identifier":"threshold-values","label":"Threshold Values","html_id":"threshold-values","implicit":true,"key":"Ode6k0l8Zm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The build up of TOX is quantized into integer points, but unlike a spell-slot like system, there is not a hard limit for ``running out’’ of the ability to cast arcana. Instead, characters have a so-called Arcanic Threshold Value, or ATV, that describes the amount of TOX they can tolerate before suffering adverse effects. One can cast past this level, but will begin to take on status conditions and other negative consequences for doing so.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"cD2Q16MSpU"}],"key":"rJSilcMJbr"},{"type":"table","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Player Level","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"DhrluY5ZIT"}],"key":"mL78WGEsaB"},{"type":"tableCell","header":true,"position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arcane TOX Value","position":{"start":{"line":13,"column":1},"end":{"line":13,"column":1}},"key":"NxUyGropqB"}],"key":"Jw5edeQSa6"}],"key":"MVYV0DU3Jh"},{"type":"tableRow","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"tableCell","position":{"start":{"line":15,"column":1},"end":{"line